frozen-as v-env
# A VARIANT, NEVER THE PRODUCT: THE GHOST BEHIND THE CAR, FOR THE WHOLE PICTURE, BY THE LIGHT THAT STAYS AT A SCREEN PLACE
# (2026-10-11; docs\reports\fg-3\desk-2026-10-11-ghost\BRIEF-env.md and READING.md, mock5.py beside them; the numbers
# of this library are in docs\reports\fg-3\desk-2026-10-11-ghost\env). IT CHANGES THE PICTURE. Built only into a variant
# library (build-ffx-own.ps1 -Variant; tools\ffx-own\build_variants.py env), FROM THE PRODUCT and not on top of v-ghost.
#
# WHAT AMD'S CODE DOES THERE. The interpolation knows one motion a pixel, the ground's. The car's shadow, glow, shading
# and reflection lie on that ground and stay with the car on the screen. So a fetched piece of ground arrives with the
# light of the place it was fetched from: a band of sunlit ground under the car, a second outline behind it.
#
# THE VARIANT, in two passes of AMD's and with no pass added:
#   THE DISOCCLUSION MASK'S PASS (one thread a pixel of the guides) also writes THE TWO ENVELOPES of the real
#     frame, AT THE SAME SCREEN PLACE frame after frame, moved by no vector, of three numbers: the log of the brightness
#     (one texel for ENV_TEXEL by ENV_TEXEL pixels, the mean of those pixels: the down-sampling is the blur), and THE
#     TINT, the log of red over brightness and of blue over brightness (one texel for twice that a side):
#         up = max(l, up_before - step)        lo = min(l, lo_before + step)
#     step is ENV_STEP of the log a real frame of 16.7 ms (it follows the frame time), OR ENV_SHARE OF WHAT IS LEFT TO
#     GO where that is less. Light that stays at a place is in both; a shadow that streams past with the ground is
#     forgotten by `up`, a passing pool of light by `lo`.
#     (TWO THINGS HERE ARE THIS LIBRARY'S OWN AND NOT THE DESK'S. The second half of the step: with the plain step a
#     texture whose own contrast is under the step is never forgotten at all, the two envelopes are then the frame
#     itself, and every piece of plain ground is "relit" for the place by its own grain; with it the gap between the
#     two envelopes is what the place has been seen to vary by, at any contrast. And the tint: a tail light's glow on
#     a wet road is a difference of COLOUR far more than of brightness, and with brightness alone the second outline
#     behind the car stays, as red as the product's.)
#     Two images a dispatch (two channels of brightness, four of tint); the frame before's are the ones the dispatch
#     before wrote (they change places at every dispatch). The first dispatch after a reset that runs this pass
#     writes the frame itself into both envelopes.
#     (WHY THIS PASS. The envelopes were first written by the optical flow field's pass, one thread for 8 by 8 pixels of
#     the display: sixteen texels one after the other in a thread, 66 us at 3840x2160. Here a thread writes one
#     texel (a thread in four also the tint's), the same numbers into the same texels; where the guides are smaller
#     than half the display a thread writes two by two of them.)
#   THE INTERPOLATION PASS, for the two colours fetched along the game's vector, each with its fetch place f and the
#     place p it is put, and for each of the three numbers: g_up = up(p) - up(f), g_lo = lo(p) - lo(f); the gain
#     needed is the smaller of the two in size where they agree in sign and 0 where they do not (the brightness's held
#     within log 1/16 and log 16, a tint's within ENV_TINT_MOST).
#     THE DEAD BAND IS NOT ONE NUMBER: a gain is believed only as far as it stands out of what the place and the fetch
#     place have themselves been seen to vary by, the gap between their two envelopes (the larger of the two gaps,
#     and ENV_GATE_WIDTH more): nothing under ENV_GATE_0 times that, whole from ENV_GATE_1 times that on. Where
#     nothing is believed the pixel takes THE PRODUCT'S PATH EXACTLY: no colour and no weight is touched.
#     Else each sample's red, green and blue are multiplied by exp(the brightness's gain and the tints' in it), and
#     where two samples are blended each one's share is multiplied by exp(-|what it needed| / ENV_TRUST): the sample
#     that needed the least relighting is believed.
#     Nothing is done in the dispatch of a reset (AMD's pass copies the real frame there) nor in the ENV_FRAME_0 frames
#     after it; whole from ENV_FRAME_1 frames after it on. Nothing is done where the game's vector is zero (the fetch
#     place is the place).
#   The two colours fetched along optical flow's own vector are left as they are (where that vector is the game's
#     they are the game's two, relit).
# A PICTURE OF sRGB VALUES (no HDR): the envelopes hold 2.2 times the logs of the raw values, and a gain is taken to the
# power 1 / 2.2 for the raw colour. NOT RUN: every captured run is HDR (scRGB).
#
# NO NEW KIND OF CALL: filtered samples of one level (SampleLevel through AMD's own linear, clamped sampler), loads,
# stores into float images of two and four channels through unordered access views that are never read (R16G16_FLOAT
# and R16G16B16A16_FLOAT, both formats AMD's own passes already write so), log, exp, smoothstep; no gather, no wave
# operation, no atomic, no typed load from an unordered access view.
what A VARIANT (the picture changes): each sample of the interpolation is relit for the place it is put, by two envelopes of the real frames' log brightness and tint kept at the screen place, where that stands out of what the two places have been seen to vary by
passes ffx_frameinterpolation_pass, ffx_frameinterpolation_disocclusion_mask_pass
wave64 the same edits in both variants: no wave operation; not run here on a wave64 device
